[interviewer · RECOMMENDATION · 8:46] Walk me through the 15-20% figure: how did you get there from 58 points back to 42? Then tell me which levers you'd consider, and whether you would pull price alone.

[candidate · 10:13] Let me redo it, I think I hand-waved. If prices go up x% and volume holds, COGS dollars stay the same but revenue scales. So 58 divided by (1+x) equals 42 means 1+x is about 1.38 — a 38% price increase. That's way more than my 15-20%, I was sloppy.

But they probably don't need to get all the way back to 24%. A 10% price rise takes COGS to about 53 points, so margin goes from 6 to maybe 11.

So no, not price alone. I'd also look at supplier contracts or hedging on beans, cheaper packaging, and maybe menu mix — pushing higher-margin items. But I'd want to know how price-sensitive their customers are before moving.
